{
  "title": "87: al-A-a'laa الأعلى",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسَبِّحِ اسْمَ رَبِّكَ الْاَعْلَىۙ‏(1)\nSABBEH ISME RABBEKAL A-A’LAL.\nHallow thou the name of thy Lord, the Most High\nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَ فَسَوّٰى ۙ‏(2)\nLAZEE KHALAQA FASAWWAA.\nHe Who createth and fashioneth (all things)\nوَالَّذِىْ قَدَّرَ فَهَدٰى ۙ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEE QADDARA FA-HADAA.\nAnd He Who planned, and guideth them\nوَالَّذِىْۤ اَخْرَجَ الْمَرْعٰى ۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAZEE AKHRAJAL MAR-A’A.\nAnd He Who bringeth forth the herbage\nفَجَعَلَهٗ غُثَآءً اَحْوٰىؕ‏(5)\nFA-JA-A’LAHU GHOSAAA-AN AHWAA.\nAnd then reduceth it to dusty stubble\nسَنُقْرِئُكَ فَلَا تَنْسٰٓىۙ‏(6)\nSANUQRE-OKA FALAA TANSAA.\nAnd We make thee to read so that thou shouldst not forget\nاِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّهٗ يَعْلَمُ الْجَهْرَ وَمَا يَخْفٰىؕ‏(7)\nILLAA MAA SHAAA-AL LAAH, INNAHU YA’LAMUL JAHRA WA MAA KAKHFAA.\nSave what willeth God; Verily He knoweth the declared and what is hidden\nوَنُيَسِّرُكَ لِلْيُسْرٰى ۖۚ‏(8)\nWA NOYASSEROKA LIL-YUSRAA.\nWe shall ease (thy way) unto an ease (for thee)\nفَذَكِّرْ اِنْ نَّفَعَتِ الذِّكْرٰىؕ‏(9)\nFA-ZAKKIR IN NAFA-A’TIZ ZIKRAA.\nAnd thou go on reminding, for it profiteth (mankind) reminding it\nسَيَذَّكَّرُ مَنْ يَّخْشٰىۙ‏(10)\nSAYAZZAKKARO MAN-Y YAKHSHAA.\nHe that feareth (God) will mind the warning\nوَيَتَجَنَّبُهَا الْاَشْقَىۙ‏(11)\nWA YATAJANNABOHAL ASQAL.\nAnd will avoid it, the most reprobate one\nالَّذِىْ يَصْلَى النَّارَ الْكُبْرٰىۚ‏(12)\nLAZEE YASLAN NAARAL KUBRAA.\nWho shall be committed to great fire\nثُمَّ لَا يَمُوْتُ فِيْهَا وَلَا يَحْيٰىؕ‏(13)\nSUMMA LAA YAMOOTO FEEHAA WA LAA YAHYAA.\nThen he shall die not therein, nor shall he live (in it)\nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ مَنْ تَزَكّٰىۙ‏(14)\nQAD AFLAHA MAN TAZAKKAA.\nIndeed he (alone) succeedeth who purifieth himself\nوَذَكَرَ اسْمَ رَبِّهٖ فَصَلّٰى ؕ‏(15)\nWA ZAKARAS MA RABBEHI FA-SALLAA.\nAnd remembereth the Name of his Lord and (regularly) prayeth\nبَلْ تُؤْثِرُوْنَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَاۖ‏(16)\nBAL TOA-SEROONAL HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nNay! prefer ye the life of this world\nوَالْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ وَّ اَبْقٰىؕ‏(17)\nWAL AAKHERATO KHAYRUNW WA ABQAA.\nAlthough the hereafter is better and more lasting\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَفِى الصُّحُفِ الْاُوْلٰىۙ‏(18)\nINNA HAAZAA LAFIS SOHOFIL OOLAA.\nVerily, this is in the scriptures earlier\nصُحُفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَمُوْسٰى‏(19)\nSOHOFE IBRAAHEEMA WA MOOSAA.\nThe Scriptures of Abraham and Moses",
  "merits": "There are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated that the reciter of this Surah will get the reward equal to ten times the number of letters in the divine books that were revealed to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), Prophet Ibrahim (a.s.) and Prophet Musa (a.s.). It is also said that in the hereafter, he will be told to enter Jannah through whichever door he pleases.\nImam Ali (a.s.) used to recite this Surah often in his compulsory prayers. Surah al-A’ala is also good for relieving ear pains and other ailments."
